  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the best areas to live in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on how you’ll use the home. Al Hamra Village suits families, golfers and investors who want tenants in place; Mina Al Arab suits families who want a quieter, low-rise lagoon community; Al Marjan Island suits buyers who want a resort-led, branded home near the Wynn resort; and Downtown RAK suits professionals who want short commutes and the lowest entry prices. RFR covers all four."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which area of Ras Al Khaimah is best for property investment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on your goal. Al Hamra Village suits investors who want tenants in place from day one, and has the deepest rental market in RAK. Al Marjan Island suits resort-led off-plan and holiday lets, and all nine off-plan launches in our book, including Manta Bay, are there. Mina Al Arab suits buyers who want space in a family-led community, and Downtown RAK has the lowest entry prices. More in our Ras Al Khaimah property investment guide."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can foreigners buy in all these areas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not all of them. Al Marjan Island (including Manta Bay), Al Hamra Village and Mina Al Arab are designated freehold areas, so foreign buyers can own property there outright. In Downtown RAK, freehold is limited to designated projects such as Julphar Towers and RAK Central. UAE and GCC nationals can buy anywhere in the Emirate. Full answer: can foreigners buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Ras Al Khaimah a good place to buy property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be, for the right buyer. Foreigners can buy freehold in designated areas, there is no income or capital gains tax on UAE property, and AED 2M of property can qualify you for a Golden Visa. But 2026 price growth slowed, more than 34,000 new homes are expected by 2030, and nobody knows what Wynn will do to prices. Read our Ras Al Khaimah property investment guide."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can foreigners buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in the designated freehold areas. Al Marjan Island, Mina Al Arab and Al Hamra Village are all freehold, so foreign buyers can own property there outright. In Downtown RAK, freehold is limited to designated projects such as Julphar Towers and RAK Central, so check the exact building before you pay a deposit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which area of Ras Al Khaimah has the highest rental yield?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Downtown RAK and Al Hamra Village show the highest indicative gross yields in our book, around 7–9%, ahead of Al Marjan Island and Mina Al Arab."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the cheapest place to buy an apartment in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Downtown RAK has the lowest entry prices in our book, with apartments from around AED 400,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which area suits families?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mina Al Arab and Al Hamra Village are the most family-led, with schools, villas and townhouses nearby; Al Hamra Village adds a golf course and marina."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which area is closest to Wynn Al Marjan Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Al Marjan Island itself is where Wynn is being built. Al Hamra Village is the closest established community, around 12 minutes away, and is where much of the resort workforce is expected to rent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the government fees when you buy in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Buyers typically pay a property registration fee to the RAK Land Department on top of the purchase price. We confirm the exact figure for any specific unit before you commit."}